1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,103
EPISODE 2

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:05,072
Leave nicely while I'm asking nicely.

3
00:00:05,138 --> 00:00:07,074
Or do you want to get beaten senseless

4
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:09,009
and leave bawling your eyes out?

5
00:00:09,076 --> 00:00:11,612
It's been so long.
Why be so cold? You're hurting me.

6
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,280
Got early-onset dementia?

7
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:15,549
Don't you remember what you did to us?

8
00:00:15,616 --> 00:00:19,086
Let's leave the past behind, my friend.

9
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:25,893
I don't have time to waste on you.

10
00:00:26,894 --> 00:00:28,729
Go out while I'm asking nicely.

11
00:00:30,898 --> 00:00:32,966
Hey, how can I go out

12
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:35,903
when I'm not even a candle?

13
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:40,474
Did you just crack a joke?

14
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:42,309
You're dead meat.

15
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:44,545
Come on, Min-ki, stop it.

16
00:00:44,611 --> 00:00:46,547
-Stop it, don't do it.
-Please calm down.

17
00:00:46,613 --> 00:00:47,548
-Let go!
-Calm down, man.

18
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:49,750
-Just calm down.
-Do I look like--

19
00:00:49,816 --> 00:00:51,251
Do I look like I can calm down?

20
00:00:51,318 --> 00:00:54,221
Don't you remember
what that bastard did to us?

21
00:00:55,022 --> 00:00:56,957
I know, I know.

22
00:00:57,024 --> 00:01:00,127
I'm not thrilled to see
that jerk's mug either.

23
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:01,328
Then why bring him?

24
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:03,063
Why did you bring him? Why!

25
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:04,731
Then what about the band?

26
00:01:04,798 --> 00:01:07,601
Where else will we find someone
as good as Hyeok for the album?

27
00:01:07,668 --> 00:01:10,237
Then we'll just be a trio!
A three-piece band!

28
00:01:10,304 --> 00:01:13,407
And the farming?
The 100,000 heads of cabbage?

29
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:26,019
HADUROK-RI

30
00:01:29,456 --> 00:01:31,692
Man, this is nice.

31
00:01:35,896 --> 00:01:38,932
This is my very own hometown,

32
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:42,202
and the dreamland
where our dreams will come true,

33
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:43,637
Hadurok-ri.

34
00:01:43,704 --> 00:01:46,039
Seriously? Hadurok-ri?

35
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:47,874
Hard Rock? Hard Rock?

36
00:01:48,742 --> 00:01:51,244
For a country village name,
it's pretty American-style.

37
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:53,847
Right? Is there a Soft Rock-ri
nearby too?

38
00:01:53,914 --> 00:01:55,849
It's nothing like that, you punk.

39
00:01:55,916 --> 00:01:59,453
There's a sad legend
behind this village's name.

40
00:02:00,187 --> 00:02:01,755
-A legend?
-Right.

41
00:02:02,356 --> 00:02:06,393
It was probably during
the Later Jin Invasion of Joseon.

42
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:08,662
ROYAL PALANQUIN

43
00:02:08,729 --> 00:02:10,297
The king was fleeing the war

44
00:02:10,364 --> 00:02:12,399
and passing through this village.

45
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:13,333
Trudge, trudge.

46
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,369
You fools! The barbarians
are right behind us!

47
00:02:15,435 --> 00:02:16,837
Hit the gas!

48
00:02:16,903 --> 00:02:18,972
Your Majesty,
we're already in top gear.

49
00:02:19,039 --> 00:02:20,607
How bitter this is!

50
00:02:20,674 --> 00:02:22,843
Fleeing from barbarians like this!

51
00:02:22,909 --> 00:02:23,977
Boo-hoo.

52
00:02:24,044 --> 00:02:27,347
How can I face
the late kings after this?

53
00:02:27,414 --> 00:02:29,816
Gotcha, King of Joseon!

54
00:02:29,883 --> 00:02:30,751
ROAR

55
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:33,387
It's the barbarians!
Protect His Majesty!

56
00:02:33,453 --> 00:02:34,788
Go, our team, go!

57
00:02:34,855 --> 00:02:38,191
V-I-C-T-O-R-Y!

58
00:02:38,258 --> 00:02:39,292
Yank!

59
00:02:39,359 --> 00:02:40,594
Yikes!

60
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:41,528
SNICKER

61
00:02:41,595 --> 00:02:42,562
Die, King of Joseon!

62
00:02:42,629 --> 00:02:43,497
SWISH

63
00:02:43,563 --> 00:02:45,432
So it's off to heaven for me.

64
00:02:45,499 --> 00:02:47,868
I should've given
more church offerings before dying.

65
00:02:47,934 --> 00:02:48,802
Huh?

66
00:02:48,869 --> 00:02:49,736
Peek.

67
00:02:49,803 --> 00:02:50,804
CRUNCH

68
00:02:50,871 --> 00:02:52,606
THUD, THUD

69
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:53,907
A deer! Aargh!

70
00:02:53,974 --> 00:02:54,841
JOSEON KING

71
00:02:54,908 --> 00:02:55,776
BAM

72
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:57,344
INSTANT GRIN

73
00:02:58,278 --> 00:02:59,613
BAM

74
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:04,618
SMIRK

75
00:03:10,023 --> 00:03:11,958
After that, the king

76
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:15,996
bestowed the Senior Second Rank
upon the sika deer that saved him,

77
00:03:16,063 --> 00:03:19,566
and that deer came to be called
Jeong-ipum-rok.

78
00:03:21,001 --> 00:03:23,503
What? Jeong-ipum-rok?

79
00:03:23,570 --> 00:03:27,274
After that, to honor
the deer's great deed,

80
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:31,845
with Du for head, Rok for deer,
and Ri for village,

81
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:35,082
it came to be called Durok-ri.

82
00:03:35,148 --> 00:03:38,685
As the village grew, it split into
Sangdurok-ri and Hadurok-ri

83
00:03:38,752 --> 00:03:40,287
as separate districts.

84
00:03:40,353 --> 00:03:42,823
Gosh, quit talking nonsense,
seriously.

85
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,825
What are you talking about right now?

86
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:46,159
Quit bluffing, you punk.

87
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,994
No! Hey, I'm not bluffing!

88
00:03:48,061 --> 00:03:51,631
Hey, I've heard of Jeongipumsong,

89
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:55,302
but never in my whole life have I heard
of Jeong-ipum-rok, you punk.

90
00:03:55,368 --> 00:03:59,172
Hey, and how could deer antlers
pierce a person's belly?

91
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,141
Human belly skin's tougher
than you think.

92
00:04:01,208 --> 00:04:03,243
Right, are antlers a spear
or a sashimi knife?

93
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:04,711
Why talk such nonsense?

94
00:04:04,778 --> 00:04:05,846
It's true!

95
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:07,914
This is driving me nuts!

96
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:11,918
Okay, you guys see that deer
in the pen over there?

97
00:04:12,452 --> 00:04:15,522
That deer is the descendant
of Jeong-ipum-rok's

98
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:18,859
descendant's, that descendant's,
descendant's next descendant's

99
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:21,128
grandson or so, that one.

100
00:04:21,194 --> 00:04:23,196
And around its neck, that…

101
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,831
That sparkling necklace!

102
00:04:24,898 --> 00:04:26,566
That necklace is none other than…

103
00:04:28,335 --> 00:04:30,804
Th-that's right, President Roh Moo-hyun

104
00:04:30,871 --> 00:04:32,606
came here himself
and put it on!

105
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:37,477
Fine, let's say that's true.

106
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:38,845
Is the cabbage patch real?

107
00:04:38,912 --> 00:04:40,080
Not a lie, right?

108
00:04:40,147 --> 00:04:41,848
I told you it's not a lie!

109
00:04:43,150 --> 00:04:46,253
You guys, I'll show you right now,

110
00:04:46,319 --> 00:04:48,054
so don't let your jaws drop.

111
00:04:56,363 --> 00:04:59,332
Well? Starting to get the picture,
gentlemen?

112
00:04:59,399 --> 00:05:03,370
This is 10,000 pyeong. Ten thousand!

113
00:05:04,004 --> 00:05:08,742
Three months from now,
this place will be packed with cabbages.

114
00:05:21,421 --> 00:05:24,691
And by the
Two-Year Cabbage Price Cycle Theory,

115
00:05:24,758 --> 00:05:28,094
cabbage prices this year
will definitely skyrocket!

116
00:05:30,764 --> 00:05:31,998
Did you see that?

117
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,502
Did you see that? Did you see it?

118
00:05:36,903 --> 00:05:41,007
After that, our Excellent Souls

119
00:05:42,375 --> 00:05:44,978
will rise again! Rise again!

120
00:05:46,279 --> 00:05:50,116
Yes! Rock and roll! Rock and roll!

121
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:53,420
You guys are in a total stew
of deep emotion.

122
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:55,455
Where's the house, though?

123
00:05:58,225 --> 00:06:01,494
Don't tell me we actually
have to live here?

124
00:06:01,561 --> 00:06:03,897
Um, it's fine, it's fine.

125
00:06:03,964 --> 00:06:07,567
Hey, despite how it looks,
it's super sturdy.

126
00:06:07,634 --> 00:06:09,035
Want to see?

127
00:06:09,903 --> 00:06:11,738
Look at this thing.

128
00:06:24,284 --> 00:06:26,253
Hey, still, man…

129
00:06:26,319 --> 00:06:30,323
As long as this roof doesn't cave in,
it's fine! Thump, thump!

130
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,665
Hey, you guys said you were hungry.
Let's eat first.

131
00:06:44,704 --> 00:06:46,206
Is this a folk village?

132
00:06:46,973 --> 00:06:50,644
Man, in Seoul, people pay good money
for cauldron rice.

133
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:52,979
It tastes out of this world!

134
00:06:53,046 --> 00:06:55,148
Just have a taste first, Gentlemen.

135
00:06:55,215 --> 00:06:56,917
There should be rice somewhere.

136
00:06:56,983 --> 00:06:58,585
Oh, here it is.

137
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:11,765
Seriously!

138
00:07:12,966 --> 00:07:15,068
It's fine, it's fine.

139
00:07:15,135 --> 00:07:18,471
Hey, if there's no rice,
we can just eat ramen!

140
00:07:18,538 --> 00:07:20,040
Should we unpack first?

141
00:07:22,909 --> 00:07:25,845
Why is it so dark in here
in broad daylight?

142
00:07:25,912 --> 00:07:28,548
It's fine, it's fine.

143
00:07:28,615 --> 00:07:30,183
This is fun, so fun.

144
00:07:32,218 --> 00:07:33,420
Did I drive too long?

145
00:07:33,486 --> 00:07:34,888
Why am I seeing things?

146
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:51,471
Stay back, stay back!

147
00:07:51,538 --> 00:07:53,206
-What is that?
-Stay back, punk!

148
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:55,275
That's a deer, right?

149
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,478
A s-s-sika deer.

150
00:07:58,545 --> 00:08:01,047
You really outdo yourself.

151
00:08:01,114 --> 00:08:04,217
A haunted house, and now
even a deer in the room, a deer!

152
00:08:06,386 --> 00:08:07,787
It's fine, it's fine.

153
00:08:07,854 --> 00:08:09,389
How is everything fine to you?

154
00:08:09,456 --> 00:08:10,523
You said it was all ready!

155
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:12,359
You said to just bring ourselves!

156
00:08:12,425 --> 00:08:13,293
Hey!

157
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,161
Hey, the countryside is all like this.

158
00:08:15,228 --> 00:08:16,830
Expecting a hotel suite?

159
00:08:16,896 --> 00:08:18,999
Whatever. I'm starving to death.

160
00:08:19,065 --> 00:08:21,134
Feed me, feed me, feed me!

161
00:08:21,201 --> 00:08:22,902
All right, fine!

162
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:24,537
I'll just go buy some ramen.

163
00:08:24,604 --> 00:08:26,306
Just unpack your stuff.

164
00:08:28,942 --> 00:08:31,478
Hey, how on earth
did that deer get in?

165
00:08:31,544 --> 00:08:32,779
The door was locked.

166
00:08:32,846 --> 00:08:35,115
Did the deer open the-- Argh!

167
00:08:39,819 --> 00:08:41,454
I was out of my mind.

168
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:44,758
I never should've trusted you
and followed you down here.

169
00:08:44,824 --> 00:08:46,760
Come on, it's still fun.

170
00:08:46,826 --> 00:08:49,295
-Feels like we're camping, right?
-Camping, my ass.

171
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,431
Feels like wilderness survival.

172
00:08:51,498 --> 00:08:54,934
Why isn't there a single store
around here?

173
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:00,573
Huh?

174
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:01,941
What? What now?

175
00:09:02,008 --> 00:09:03,410
A diner? A diner? A diner?

176
00:09:05,145 --> 00:09:07,814
Wow, this place is still here.

177
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:10,483
-What is this place?
-My old elementary school.

178
00:09:11,151 --> 00:09:14,554
An elementary school?
You call this tiny thing a school?

179
00:09:14,621 --> 00:09:16,623
Rural branch schools are like that.

180
00:09:16,689 --> 00:09:19,626
There were maybe ten students in total.

181
00:09:21,428 --> 00:09:23,163
I wonder if it's still there.

182
00:09:28,001 --> 00:09:30,003
YUN-HUI ♡ MIN-GI

183
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:41,214
Yun-hui was an older woman,
3 years older than me.

184
00:09:41,281 --> 00:09:45,418
Long straight hair, fair skin,
and a slender figure.

185
00:09:46,186 --> 00:09:48,888
Smart, and great at piano too.

186
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,093
Every single boy had a crush on her.

187
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:55,728
And then one day,

188
00:09:55,795 --> 00:09:58,431
something fateful happened.

189
00:10:08,241 --> 00:10:09,909
Go ahead.

190
00:10:19,152 --> 00:10:20,587
Help!

191
00:10:21,888 --> 00:10:22,989
Help me!

192
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:28,228
Help, I can't swim!

193
00:10:28,862 --> 00:10:30,497
Help!

194
00:10:52,852 --> 00:10:54,287
Are you okay?

195
00:10:54,354 --> 00:10:55,321
Yes.

196
00:10:55,388 --> 00:10:57,724
Thank goodness.

197
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:03,997
And that's how our fateful love
began.

198
00:11:06,866 --> 00:11:10,103
But as first loves always go,

199
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,038
ours was never meant to be.

200
00:11:12,805 --> 00:11:15,942
Soon after, my mom dragged me off
to Seoul,

201
00:11:17,143 --> 00:11:21,347
and we could never meet again.

202
00:11:29,455 --> 00:11:31,391
That is so unbelievably…

203
00:11:32,559 --> 00:11:33,893
cliché, totally cliché.

204
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:38,498
Anyway, I wonder where Yun-hui is
and what she's doing now.

205
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,436
Hey, you little punk, stop right there!

206
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,108
Easy, easy.

207
00:11:49,175 --> 00:11:50,343
You little bastard!

208
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:51,844
Got you.

209
00:11:56,349 --> 00:11:58,484
That's it! Now, grab it now!

210
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,619
It's okay, it's okay.

211
00:11:59,686 --> 00:12:02,255
It's okay, it's okay, easy now.

212
00:12:02,322 --> 00:12:03,756
Oh dear, Father.

213
00:12:04,624 --> 00:12:05,892
Come to big sis.

214
00:12:05,959 --> 00:12:08,995
Come here, little piggy,
little piggy, little piggy!

215
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:13,499
Why, you little piggy--

216
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:22,275
Acting so feisty for a little thing.

217
00:12:29,115 --> 00:12:31,985
Oh, thank goodness, Father.

218
00:12:32,885 --> 00:12:33,886
Good work, Yun-hui.

219
00:12:33,953 --> 00:12:36,289
Oh, it was nothing at all.

220
00:12:37,323 --> 00:12:39,125
County Governor's coming tomorrow.

221
00:12:39,192 --> 00:12:40,660
Of course I know.

222
00:12:40,727 --> 00:12:44,430
Yun-hui, how did our Kkotdori get
picked as the county mascot?

223
00:12:44,497 --> 00:12:45,431
I know, right?

224
00:12:45,498 --> 00:12:48,601
They say the prize money is huge.

225
00:12:48,668 --> 00:12:50,103
Kkotdori saved our project

226
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:52,572
We're finally going to pave our road!

227
00:12:52,639 --> 00:12:54,907
Anyway, we have to clean
the village tomorrow,

228
00:12:54,974 --> 00:12:56,743
so gather here by dawn, okay?

229
00:12:57,543 --> 00:13:02,081
What great weather.
Perfect for ripening rice.

230
00:13:02,148 --> 00:13:03,283
Oh, there's Mr. Heo.

231
00:13:03,349 --> 00:13:05,752
Mr. Heo! Is it going well?

232
00:13:05,818 --> 00:13:07,253
Did you pull out a lot?

233
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:13,660
Oh my, Mr. Heo's hen, Gyesun,
has grown so much.

234
00:13:14,427 --> 00:13:17,430
Hens really are meant to lay eggs.

235
00:13:17,497 --> 00:13:21,534
Ma'am! Amazing weather today, right?

236
00:13:25,705 --> 00:13:28,174
Does this town even have a store?

237
00:13:28,241 --> 00:13:30,810
Jeez, stop whining, you punk.

238
00:13:30,877 --> 00:13:33,913
What town doesn't have a store
these days?

239
00:13:37,550 --> 00:13:38,985
Hey, kid!

240
00:13:40,787 --> 00:13:42,255
Where's the store in town?

241
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:45,425
There isn't one.
You have to go to the township.

242
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,727
What? There isn't one?

243
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:51,531
How far is the township?

244
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:53,866
Um, about 40 minutes by bus?

245
00:13:56,235 --> 00:13:57,770
Forty minutes?

246
00:13:57,837 --> 00:14:00,206
This is driving me crazy.

247
00:14:01,274 --> 00:14:04,210
Anyway, thanks, kid.

248
00:14:06,746 --> 00:14:08,247
Jeez, find a restaurant then.

249
00:14:08,314 --> 00:14:09,916
I'm starving to death.

250
00:14:09,982 --> 00:14:12,218
With no store, would there be a diner?

251
00:14:12,285 --> 00:14:13,319
Think before you talk.

252
00:14:13,386 --> 00:14:15,621
I don't care. I'm starving to death.

253
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:18,257
Huh?

254
00:14:26,466 --> 00:14:30,169
Those… are apples, right?

255
00:14:30,903 --> 00:14:34,340
Wow, they look so good, right?

256
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,381
-Want some?
-Yes!

257
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,118
Follow me.

258
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:46,052
Where?

259
00:14:46,119 --> 00:14:47,787
Don't tell me we're stealing them?

260
00:14:47,854 --> 00:14:49,889
Stealing? Come on.

261
00:14:49,956 --> 00:14:51,924
It's crop-pinching, you punk.

262
00:14:52,592 --> 00:14:55,661
A beautiful rural tradition
you can't see in Seoul.

263
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:57,930
It's a kind of game.

264
00:14:58,598 --> 00:15:00,199
Still, I don't think we should…

265
00:15:00,266 --> 00:15:02,268
It's fine, really.

266
00:15:02,335 --> 00:15:06,572
Back in my prime,
I was the King of Crop-Pinching.

267
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:09,876
Trust me and follow me.
We won't get caught.

268
00:15:09,942 --> 00:15:11,310
Come on.

269
00:15:11,377 --> 00:15:13,246
Hey, wait!

270
00:15:13,312 --> 00:15:15,915
-Follow me.
-Don't go, you punk!

271
00:15:16,983 --> 00:15:20,553
This'll be fun.
I always wanted to try crop-pinching.

272
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:30,263
Whatever.

273
00:16:01,527 --> 00:16:04,430
-Here, eat.
-Really?

274
00:16:04,497 --> 00:16:06,065
Thanks, Min-ki.

275
00:16:12,538 --> 00:16:15,341
This is super delicious!
Is this really an apple?

276
00:16:15,942 --> 00:16:19,145
Quit making a fuss, you jerk.
Apples all taste the same. Give it.

277
00:16:20,246 --> 00:16:23,216
Whoa! It's nothing like
the ones in Seoul.

278
00:16:23,883 --> 00:16:27,520
Of course, you punk.
Nothing beats freshly picked ones.

279
00:16:27,587 --> 00:16:30,656
Once you eat these and go back up
to Seoul to eat other apples,

280
00:16:30,723 --> 00:16:32,358
you'll never eat them again.

281
00:16:32,425 --> 00:16:34,393
What's keeping you? Dig in!

282
00:16:36,562 --> 00:16:39,398
Hey, pick the red ones!

283
00:16:39,465 --> 00:16:41,000
Min-ki!

284
00:16:41,067 --> 00:16:43,536
Hyeok, pick that one up there.

285
00:16:43,603 --> 00:16:44,470
-Up there?
-Red one.

286
00:16:44,537 --> 00:16:46,639
-Thanks. I can't reach.
-Got it!

287
00:16:47,707 --> 00:16:48,708
This one too.

288
00:16:48,774 --> 00:16:51,244
I can't reach it.

289
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:53,379
Right here, up top.

290
00:16:53,446 --> 00:16:54,847
Is it okay to do this?

291
00:16:54,914 --> 00:16:57,049
It's fine.
That's what crop-pinching is.

292
00:16:57,116 --> 00:16:59,185
-Nobody's here.
-So good!

293
00:16:59,252 --> 00:17:01,120
Hey, pick the red ones!

294
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:02,555
Not that one.

295
00:17:02,622 --> 00:17:04,457
-Pick the red ones.
-The red ones?

296
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,161
Stop, I can't reach it.

297
00:17:10,897 --> 00:17:13,332
-Min-ki, give me one too.
-Like this one.

298
00:17:15,601 --> 00:17:17,670
You have to pick ones like this.

299
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:26,979
The apples…
just looked so delicious…

300
00:17:28,347 --> 00:17:29,849
We weren't stealing…

301
00:17:29,916 --> 00:17:31,984
That country custom, uh…

302
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,986
-Seori, seori.
-A game!

303
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,421
Seori, seori, seori!

304
00:18:33,245 --> 00:18:35,915
We really almost died.

305
00:18:37,083 --> 00:18:39,485
Seori, my foot!
A lovely country custom?

306
00:18:39,552 --> 00:18:40,586
Just a game?!

307
00:18:40,653 --> 00:18:43,489
Since when did country hospitality
get so brutal?

308
00:18:45,358 --> 00:18:47,293
What's this? It's crap!

309
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:49,428
-Crap?
-Yes!

310
00:18:51,664 --> 00:18:52,932
Man, seriously…

311
00:18:58,771 --> 00:19:02,842
This won't even come out.
It was an authentic birthday gift.

312
00:19:02,908 --> 00:19:04,543
Damn it, seriously.

313
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:06,812
Be glad you're alive,
you punk.

314
00:19:06,879 --> 00:19:08,781
If he'd caught us,
by now we'd be

315
00:19:08,848 --> 00:19:10,282
six feet under, smelling incense…

316
00:19:43,783 --> 00:19:46,318
Hey, why aren't you working?

317
00:19:46,986 --> 00:19:50,056
I'll ruin my nails.
I paid 50,000 won for them.

318
00:19:50,122 --> 00:19:51,457
Fifty thousand won?

319
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:53,626
You paid 50,000 won
for that junk?

320
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:56,862
Everyone my age gets them done.
You wouldn't know.

321
00:19:56,929 --> 00:19:59,498
Hey, Hwang Man-sun!

322
00:19:59,565 --> 00:20:01,767
Don't call me Man-sun!

323
00:20:01,834 --> 00:20:03,836
I'm I-ji now. Hwang I-ji.

324
00:20:03,903 --> 00:20:06,305
You crazy girl.

325
00:20:06,372 --> 00:20:08,974
She doesn't know
the value of money.

326
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,744
You got Botox yesterday, Mom.

327
00:20:11,811 --> 00:20:12,678
What?

328
00:20:12,745 --> 00:20:13,612
Again?

329
00:20:13,679 --> 00:20:16,949
Why, that…
That big-mouthed girl!

330
00:20:17,016 --> 00:20:19,919
So that's why you've been wearing
this ridiculous hat.

331
00:20:19,985 --> 00:20:20,986
Oh, Mama!

332
00:20:22,722 --> 00:20:23,589
Mama?

333
00:20:23,656 --> 00:20:26,358
How much younger
are you trying to get?

334
00:20:26,425 --> 00:20:27,893
Look at your son's face!

335
00:20:28,661 --> 00:20:32,298
You keep getting younger,
and your son keeps getting older.

336
00:20:32,364 --> 00:20:36,235
People still think you're my wife,
you know that?

337
00:20:37,002 --> 00:20:40,072
Then you should try Botox too.
The results are just…

338
00:20:40,139 --> 00:20:42,775
Snap out of it! Seriously!

339
00:20:42,842 --> 00:20:45,611
Do you want to end up broke
like the old days?

340
00:20:45,678 --> 00:20:48,247
Snap out of it!

341
00:20:48,881 --> 00:20:51,317
Hwang Man-sun, go get married!

342
00:20:51,383 --> 00:20:55,454
Stop driving me crazy
and get married already!

343
00:20:55,521 --> 00:20:57,923
I want to get married too!

344
00:20:57,990 --> 00:21:00,192
In this dump full of old men,

345
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,560
who's there to marry?

346
00:21:01,627 --> 00:21:03,963
If there is one, bring him here!

347
00:21:10,236 --> 00:21:11,904
Um… No way.

348
00:21:11,971 --> 00:21:13,005
Did he bring them?

349
00:21:13,072 --> 00:21:14,240
Who are you guys?

350
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:16,575
Are you perverts?

351
00:21:16,642 --> 00:21:19,645
S-sir, n-no, it's not that.
We were just…

352
00:21:26,185 --> 00:21:27,653
Don't step on them!

353
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:30,289
Don't step there!

354
00:21:30,356 --> 00:21:32,024
Don't step on them!

355
00:21:34,093 --> 00:21:36,529
Those crazy punks!
You're dead meat today!

356
00:21:37,563 --> 00:21:40,232
Just draw a chalk outline
and it's a crime scene.

357
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:41,634
A total crime scene.

358
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:43,269
Oh, Father…

359
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:45,204
Huh? What?

360
00:21:45,271 --> 00:21:47,306
Not you, Father.

361
00:21:47,373 --> 00:21:49,542
Our Father up in heaven.

362
00:21:49,608 --> 00:21:51,010
Oh, that Father?

363
00:21:53,445 --> 00:21:54,547
Hey, Sang-deuk.

364
00:21:54,613 --> 00:21:57,249
Hey, get up. Come on, get up.

365
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:58,918
Yes.

366
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:01,687
Yes, I would truly love
to get married.

367
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:09,395
-Mom…
-You want to get married?

368
00:22:09,461 --> 00:22:11,597
Then quit drinking, you idiot!

369
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:13,799
You drink like this
day in and day out.

370
00:22:13,866 --> 00:22:15,968
You couldn't even find a wife
in Vietnam,

371
00:22:16,035 --> 00:22:17,803
living in this pathetic state!

372
00:22:19,371 --> 00:22:21,140
-Oh, Father…
-Huh? What?

373
00:22:22,575 --> 00:22:24,176
Not you, Father.

374
00:22:24,243 --> 00:22:26,011
Our Father up in heaven.

375
00:22:26,745 --> 00:22:28,581
Oh, Mama! Oh, Father!

376
00:22:34,453 --> 00:22:36,522
I've never seen those faces before.

377
00:22:36,589 --> 00:22:40,492
Wait, aren't those Man-gu and Mr. Han
chasing after them?

378
00:22:40,559 --> 00:22:43,128
Leave them be. Just leave them.

379
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:46,131
They do this all the time.

380
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:49,235
They're just losing their temper
over nothing again.

381
00:22:49,301 --> 00:22:51,270
People should, you know?

382
00:22:51,337 --> 00:22:53,505
Stay calm and keep their temper…

383
00:22:58,944 --> 00:23:01,080
My makgeolli!

384
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:09,922
Stop right there, bastards!

385
00:23:12,157 --> 00:23:14,026
What? What on earth is that?

386
00:23:14,693 --> 00:23:16,562
-Hey!
-Move, move!

387
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:18,831
Get out of the way! Move!

388
00:23:20,599 --> 00:23:22,501
Stop right there, you bastards!

389
00:23:24,136 --> 00:23:25,271
My makgeolli!

390
00:23:27,973 --> 00:23:28,941
It's freezing.

391
00:23:29,008 --> 00:23:30,776
What is all this?

392
00:23:32,344 --> 00:23:33,846
-Let go of me!
-Get out of the way!

393
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:37,549
Hey, let go! Seriously,
please let go!

394
00:23:37,616 --> 00:23:38,717
What's that?

395
00:23:41,287 --> 00:23:43,689
Hey, you crazy bastards!

396
00:23:56,368 --> 00:23:58,637
You crazy bastards!
What's your deal?

397
00:23:58,704 --> 00:24:00,139
What about my ATV?

398
00:24:00,205 --> 00:24:01,507
Well? What's the plan?

399
00:24:01,573 --> 00:24:04,643
Forget the talk and call the cops!

400
00:24:04,710 --> 00:24:06,378
Lock these thieves up!

401
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:08,547
Thieves? It's a misunderstanding!

402
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:10,215
Yeah, right. Misunderstanding, my foot.

403
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:12,117
Save it for the police, you punk!

404
00:24:12,184 --> 00:24:13,886
Sang-deuk, tell it to the cops.

405
00:24:13,953 --> 00:24:15,621
It really is a mistake, mister.

406
00:24:15,688 --> 00:24:16,722
Wait a second.

407
00:24:18,524 --> 00:24:20,826
Wait, why are you…

408
00:24:20,893 --> 00:24:22,761
Mister!

409
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:24,830
What? Do you know this guy?

410
00:24:24,897 --> 00:24:27,533
He's the grandson of Grandma Kim,
who passed away recently.

411
00:24:27,599 --> 00:24:30,169
This is Min-gi.

412
00:24:30,235 --> 00:24:31,704
Min-gi?

413
00:24:31,770 --> 00:24:34,440
This guy is Min-gi?

414
00:24:34,506 --> 00:24:35,507
You know me?

415
00:24:35,574 --> 00:24:36,642
Don't you remember her?

416
00:24:36,709 --> 00:24:39,011
You followed her everywhere, man.

417
00:24:39,078 --> 00:24:40,779
Always calling out, "Yun-hui!"

418
00:24:43,382 --> 00:24:45,117
What did you say?

419
00:24:45,184 --> 00:24:46,418
Yun-hui?

420
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:47,519
Yep.

421
00:24:49,688 --> 00:24:51,357
This woman?

422
00:24:56,495 --> 00:24:58,263
No way.

423
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:01,266
My goodness, he's grown so much.

424
00:25:01,333 --> 00:25:03,135
You used to have a runny nose.

425
00:25:03,202 --> 00:25:04,837
That feels like just yesterday.

426
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:06,305
Look how much you've grown!

427
00:25:06,972 --> 00:25:08,807
So what brings you out here?

428
00:25:08,874 --> 00:25:12,444
Well, I just thought
I'd try my hand at farming.

429
00:25:12,511 --> 00:25:15,214
Forget it. I've heard enough.

430
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:17,416
Just call the police already!

431
00:25:17,483 --> 00:25:19,018
Come on, man.

432
00:25:19,084 --> 00:25:20,719
We used to be neighbors, man.

433
00:25:20,786 --> 00:25:22,021
Don't be so heartless.

434
00:25:22,087 --> 00:25:24,890
Neighbors, my foot!
Who's a neighbor here?

435
00:25:24,957 --> 00:25:27,126
These punks are bad news from the start.

436
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,794
Haven't you seen guys like this?

437
00:25:28,861 --> 00:25:30,629
I've seen plenty of them.

438
00:25:30,696 --> 00:25:33,532
When things don't pan out in the city,

439
00:25:33,599 --> 00:25:36,335
they ditch it all
and come down here to farm,

440
00:25:36,402 --> 00:25:38,537
just half-assing it for a month or two.

441
00:25:38,604 --> 00:25:41,440
Then they all turn tail and run.

442
00:25:41,507 --> 00:25:42,975
Think farming is a joke?

443
00:25:43,042 --> 00:25:45,244
Think moving to a farm is a trend?

444
00:25:45,310 --> 00:25:47,112
These guys are so predictable.

445
00:25:47,179 --> 00:25:49,581
So before they ruin our village,

446
00:25:49,648 --> 00:25:51,850
just kick them out, you bastard!

447
00:25:51,917 --> 00:25:55,687
Come on, man! We'll have to wait and see
how they do, you bastard!

448
00:25:55,754 --> 00:25:57,122
Knock it off, both of you.

449
00:25:57,790 --> 00:26:01,493
Making a scene right before
tomorrow's big event?

450
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:03,429
Village Head, sort this out.

451
00:26:03,495 --> 00:26:06,432
Yun-hui, you decide. It's your call.

452
00:26:06,498 --> 00:26:08,367
Why would Yun-hui…

453
00:26:10,369 --> 00:26:13,439
Don't tell me you're the Village Head?

454
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:17,976
No way.

455
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:21,413
My first love isn't just
some country girl,

456
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,882
she's an unmarried rural Village Head!

457
00:26:26,819 --> 00:26:30,422
Jeez, why steal apples
instead of just asking for a few?

458
00:26:31,190 --> 00:26:34,793
Why farm all of a sudden?
Did you move out to the country?

459
00:26:34,860 --> 00:26:36,595
Not for good.

460
00:26:40,132 --> 00:26:44,903
I'm actually a singer in Seoul.

461
00:26:45,704 --> 00:26:47,072
A rock band.

462
00:26:48,006 --> 00:26:50,209
We're pretty famous in Seoul.

463
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:51,810
Lately, all over the place,

464
00:26:51,877 --> 00:26:53,946
I've been getting tons of offers,

465
00:26:54,012 --> 00:26:56,949
so to sort out my thoughts
and clear my head,

466
00:26:57,015 --> 00:26:58,684
I came down for a bit.

467
00:26:58,750 --> 00:27:00,452
Oh, really?

468
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:05,324
How did you become Village Head…

469
00:27:06,325 --> 00:27:07,693
Me?

470
00:27:07,759 --> 00:27:11,430
It just kind of happened.

471
00:27:16,602 --> 00:27:19,304
Hey, you're that little kid from before.

472
00:27:21,406 --> 00:27:26,178
Great-uncle says to come eat,
but tell him you already ate.

473
00:27:26,245 --> 00:27:29,014
Great-aunt cooked again.

474
00:27:29,081 --> 00:27:31,083
Again? Wait, why?

475
00:27:32,284 --> 00:27:33,952
This is driving me crazy.

476
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:36,788
Okay, got it.
Head back first.

477
00:27:36,855 --> 00:27:39,391
-Okay, hurry home.
-Sure.

478
00:27:42,361 --> 00:27:44,796
Who's that? Your nephew?

479
00:27:44,863 --> 00:27:46,198
He's my son.

480
00:27:46,265 --> 00:27:48,967
Your son? You got married?

481
00:27:49,034 --> 00:27:49,935
No.

482
00:27:50,602 --> 00:27:52,437
What? You said he's your son!

483
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:55,374
Do you have to get married
to have a kid?

484
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:58,277
No way, you're an unwed mom?

485
00:27:59,211 --> 00:28:00,579
Well, that's…

486
00:28:00,646 --> 00:28:03,649
One thing led to another,
and it just turned out that way.

487
00:28:04,416 --> 00:28:06,151
No way!

488
00:28:06,218 --> 00:28:09,655
My first love isn't even
an unmarried Village Head,

489
00:28:09,721 --> 00:28:12,024
she's an unwed mom Village Head!

490
00:28:12,090 --> 00:28:14,693
Anyway, I'll let this slide today,

491
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:17,296
but go apologize to him later.

492
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:19,898
Apologize for what?
It was just a harmless prank.

493
00:28:19,965 --> 00:28:21,133
What's that measly stuff worth?

494
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:23,869
Did you just call it
measly stuff?

495
00:28:23,936 --> 00:28:26,171
I'll pay for it, okay? I'll pay!

496
00:28:26,238 --> 00:28:29,508
To you guys, they might just be
a few apples and flowers,

497
00:28:29,575 --> 00:28:31,944
but we poured buckets of sweat
in the blazing sun

498
00:28:32,010 --> 00:28:34,012
raising them like our own kids
since spring!

499
00:28:34,079 --> 00:28:36,915
And what? Measly stuff, you punk?

500
00:28:36,982 --> 00:28:38,350
Why throw such a fit?

501
00:28:38,417 --> 00:28:40,719
How can you farm
with that rotten attitude?

502
00:28:40,786 --> 00:28:42,654
Grow up already, grow up!

503
00:28:44,356 --> 00:28:46,225
What did I do to make you blow up?

504
00:28:46,291 --> 00:28:47,826
Jeez!

505
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:50,596
I'm so pissed off!

506
00:28:50,662 --> 00:28:51,563
Hey!

507
00:29:02,975 --> 00:29:04,977
Honey!

508
00:29:09,681 --> 00:29:10,549
Yes?

509
00:29:10,616 --> 00:29:14,987
I'm quite curious
what's in this pot.

510
00:29:15,053 --> 00:29:18,757
Oh, this?
It's soy-marinated crab spicy stew.

511
00:29:18,824 --> 00:29:21,727
Soy-marinated crab spicy stew?

512
00:29:21,793 --> 00:29:24,162
Yes, yesterday, the Women's
Association President

513
00:29:24,229 --> 00:29:26,698
made soy-marinated crab
and gave us some.

514
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:29,801
Then I suddenly craved
spicy seafood stew today.

515
00:29:29,868 --> 00:29:34,239
So I added seasoning and boiled it.
Doesn't it look delicious?

516
00:29:34,306 --> 00:29:37,643
Why go through all the trouble
of cooking, honey?

517
00:29:37,709 --> 00:29:40,012
To me, the instant food you make

518
00:29:40,078 --> 00:29:42,447
is the best in the world, I tell you.

519
00:29:44,149 --> 00:29:46,785
Still, we can't eat ramen every day.

520
00:29:46,852 --> 00:29:50,155
Come on, everyone, eat up
before it gets cold.

521
00:29:53,325 --> 00:29:55,260
Let's all choke it down.

522
00:29:55,327 --> 00:29:58,230
Don't let your guard down.
Brace yourselves, okay?

523
00:30:12,377 --> 00:30:15,981
Sweetie, what's wrong with your dad?
Did something bad happen?

524
00:30:16,048 --> 00:30:20,152
I'm not sure.
I'll go ask him.

525
00:30:22,754 --> 00:30:24,389
Dad!

526
00:30:26,224 --> 00:30:29,161
Um, why is Yun-hui so late?

527
00:30:29,227 --> 00:30:31,196
I should go check on her.

528
00:30:31,263 --> 00:30:32,464
Uncle, I'll come too.

529
00:30:32,531 --> 00:30:34,499
You too? You just eat.

530
00:30:34,566 --> 00:30:38,370
There she comes.
Great timing, Yun-hui.

531
00:30:38,437 --> 00:30:41,506
I heard some weirdos came from Seoul.

532
00:30:41,573 --> 00:30:43,942
No, just a kid who used to live here.

533
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:47,012
Good to hear.

534
00:30:47,079 --> 00:30:49,548
Hungry? Come eat.

535
00:30:49,614 --> 00:30:50,816
Huh?

536
00:30:52,551 --> 00:30:55,020
I… I already ate.

537
00:30:55,087 --> 00:30:57,289
At the village hall…
Did I have two bowls or three?

538
00:30:57,356 --> 00:30:59,725
Right, I had four bowls.
I'm so full.

539
00:30:59,791 --> 00:31:01,827
Enjoy your meal, everyone!

540
00:31:11,737 --> 00:31:13,772
What's wrong with that guy Min-gi…

541
00:31:13,839 --> 00:31:16,041
He hasn't changed a bit.
Not one bit.

542
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:21,113
Where did I put my farming log?

543
00:31:24,816 --> 00:31:26,885
What's this?

544
00:31:31,590 --> 00:31:33,525
MY SCHOOL LIFE

545
00:31:44,336 --> 00:31:47,272
Gosh, so pretty. Just so pretty.

546
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:04,756
I dedicate this song
to my beloved Yun-hui.

547
00:32:05,424 --> 00:32:07,659
From your forever white knight, Min-gi

548
00:32:07,726 --> 00:32:08,860
YUN-HUI ♡ MIN-GI

549
00:32:24,609 --> 00:32:26,778
Oh, Yun-hui

550
00:32:28,213 --> 00:32:30,148
Oh, Yun-hui

551
00:32:34,152 --> 00:32:35,854
Oh, Yun-hui

552
00:32:36,888 --> 00:32:40,025
Still, he was so cute as a kid.

553
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:43,862
Wow, it's really pretty.

554
00:32:45,030 --> 00:32:47,632
This town is really growing on me.

555
00:32:47,699 --> 00:32:49,935
We should go fishing here next time.

556
00:32:50,001 --> 00:32:52,204
Slice me some sashimi
with what I catch!

557
00:32:52,270 --> 00:32:53,305
-Sashimi?
-Yes.

558
00:32:53,371 --> 00:32:54,706
Slice it yourself, punk.

559
00:32:54,773 --> 00:32:56,007
I just like eating it.

560
00:32:56,074 --> 00:32:57,909
-Ask Han-cheol to--
-Hey!

561
00:32:59,444 --> 00:33:03,048
Wait… Are you still mad?

562
00:33:03,815 --> 00:33:06,318
I said I'm sorry. I won't do it again.

563
00:33:10,622 --> 00:33:12,457
Save it.

564
00:33:12,524 --> 00:33:14,793
I'm warning you.
If this happens one more time,

565
00:33:14,860 --> 00:33:18,196
I'm going right back to Seoul,
got it?

566
00:33:18,263 --> 00:33:19,164
Remember that.

567
00:33:19,231 --> 00:33:20,665
Fine, I got it.

568
00:33:21,666 --> 00:33:25,337
Why are you so prickly lately?
Smile a little.

569
00:33:34,646 --> 00:33:38,283
That jerk keeps making me worry.

570
00:33:40,619 --> 00:33:42,220
I need to pee.

571
00:33:51,263 --> 00:33:54,866
Call yourself a man with that trickle?

572
00:33:55,834 --> 00:33:58,203
Someone who still thinks
your pee stream

573
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:00,405
measures your stamina actually exists.

574
00:34:01,339 --> 00:34:05,377
A real man's stream should be at least…

575
00:34:17,489 --> 00:34:18,657
Why smile, punk?

576
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:19,991
Why're you smiling, punk?

577
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:21,993
Someone who still thinks
that measures stamina!

578
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:23,762
You ignorant fool!

579
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:26,798
What's that now?

580
00:34:31,670 --> 00:34:33,171
WARNING: PROTECTED RESERVOIR

581
00:34:33,238 --> 00:34:34,472
USED FOR DRINKING WATER…

582
00:34:34,539 --> 00:34:37,475
They peed in our drinking water!

583
00:34:38,343 --> 00:34:40,045
What did I tell you?

584
00:34:40,111 --> 00:34:42,380
Didn't I say to hand these punks
over to the cops?

585
00:34:42,447 --> 00:34:45,050
Hey, Village Head!
You said you'd take responsibility!

586
00:34:45,116 --> 00:34:46,718
Didn't you?

587
00:34:46,785 --> 00:34:47,886
-I'm sorry.
-Save it.

588
00:34:48,553 --> 00:34:51,923
I said a greenhorn Village Head
wouldn't work, but you picked her!

589
00:34:51,990 --> 00:34:53,558
Serves you right!

590
00:34:53,625 --> 00:34:57,495
Hey, Yun-hui didn't do anything wrong.

591
00:34:57,562 --> 00:34:59,898
They said they didn't know.

592
00:34:59,965 --> 00:35:02,701
Drop it and let's go get rice wine.

593
00:35:04,569 --> 00:35:08,206
It's on me, buddy. Hurry up and come.

594
00:35:08,273 --> 00:35:09,941
Choke on it yourself!

595
00:35:10,775 --> 00:35:12,410
You come too, In-gi.

596
00:35:21,853 --> 00:35:24,022
What the heck is wrong with you?

597
00:35:24,089 --> 00:35:25,824
I told you to be careful hours ago,

598
00:35:25,890 --> 00:35:26,758
and now this!

599
00:35:26,825 --> 00:35:28,960
I really didn't know!

600
00:35:29,027 --> 00:35:31,196
They should've made a bigger sign!

601
00:35:31,262 --> 00:35:33,531
You won't even apologize
once to the very end?

602
00:35:33,598 --> 00:35:35,367
Now that the whole village
hates you,

603
00:35:35,433 --> 00:35:36,801
how on earth will you farm?

604
00:35:36,868 --> 00:35:39,471
Why don't you just quit everything
and go back to Seoul now?

605
00:35:39,537 --> 00:35:40,905
Who are you to tell me to leave?

606
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:42,407
I'm farming on my own land.

607
00:35:42,474 --> 00:35:44,242
I'm worried you'll regret it later.

608
00:35:45,210 --> 00:35:47,646
Thank you so very much for your concern.

609
00:35:47,712 --> 00:35:49,280
But we can do great on our own.

610
00:35:49,347 --> 00:35:52,484
I don't plan on getting even a tiny bit
of help from you,

611
00:35:52,550 --> 00:35:54,986
-so mind your own business.
-Oh, is that so?

612
00:35:55,053 --> 00:35:57,188
Then I'll just wait and see
how well you do.

613
00:35:57,255 --> 00:35:59,658
Just you dare cause trouble one more time.

614
00:35:59,724 --> 00:36:01,226
You'll pay for it, got it?

615
00:36:01,292 --> 00:36:03,428
Whatever.

616
00:36:04,129 --> 00:36:05,597
Good grief, seriously!

617
00:36:13,872 --> 00:36:16,274
Who is she to butt in like that?

618
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:17,609
Move aside.

619
00:36:17,676 --> 00:36:19,244
-What is this doing here?
-I'm exhausted.

620
00:36:24,983 --> 00:36:27,285
Ow, it stings! It stings!

621
00:36:27,352 --> 00:36:28,353
It stings.

622
00:36:28,420 --> 00:36:31,289
Why is it still in there?
You said it'd leave if we opened the door!

623
00:36:31,356 --> 00:36:33,158
What can I do if it won't leave?

624
00:36:33,224 --> 00:36:36,861
Wait, then where are we sleeping tonight?

625
00:36:42,333 --> 00:36:44,669
This is all your fault, you punk.

626
00:36:47,138 --> 00:36:49,307
I can't even get out of this place.

627
00:36:58,616 --> 00:37:01,352
Farming, my foot.

628
00:37:24,442 --> 00:37:27,812
-Where are you going?
-To get some water.

629
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:44,229
CHEONGAM PHARMACY

630
00:38:04,716 --> 00:38:06,718
BUCKET LIST
1. TELL MOM I LOVE HER

631
00:38:06,785 --> 00:38:07,819
2. MATCHING DATE

632
00:38:11,055 --> 00:38:12,690
Seriously…

633
00:38:14,325 --> 00:38:17,262
Am I going to die
without ever falling in love?

634
00:38:20,565 --> 00:38:24,402
I never even dated once
and worked myself half to death, so why…

635
00:38:25,370 --> 00:38:28,506
Why me? Why on earth is it me?

636
00:38:31,342 --> 00:38:35,380
Why do I have to die
when even pests like those are alive?

637
00:38:50,862 --> 00:38:53,665
All right, let's get started.

638
00:38:53,731 --> 00:38:56,234
Hold on, let's put on sunscreen first.

639
00:38:56,301 --> 00:38:58,970
Hey, pop culture artists like us

640
00:38:59,037 --> 00:39:00,638
may have to work hard,

641
00:39:00,705 --> 00:39:02,974
but we still need
to take care of our looks.

642
00:39:03,641 --> 00:39:05,410
Come on, slather it on thick.

643
00:39:08,613 --> 00:39:09,914
-Here.
-I'll pass.

644
00:39:09,981 --> 00:39:11,883
Real men don't wear sunscreen.

645
00:39:17,689 --> 00:39:19,490
So where do we start?

646
00:39:20,558 --> 00:39:21,426
Huh?

647
00:39:21,492 --> 00:39:23,561
To grow cabbages, what do we do first?

648
00:39:23,628 --> 00:39:26,631
Uh, just a moment.

649
00:39:31,169 --> 00:39:33,204
HOW TO GROW CABBAGES

650
00:39:41,412 --> 00:39:42,847
Are you looking it up?

651
00:39:42,914 --> 00:39:45,316
You told us to farm cabbages
without knowing how?

652
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:48,253
Hey, I've lived in Seoul for 17 years too.

653
00:39:48,319 --> 00:39:49,954
I've never grown a potted plant.

654
00:39:50,021 --> 00:39:51,089
How would I know?

655
00:39:51,155 --> 00:39:52,857
Man, I swear…

656
00:39:53,658 --> 00:39:54,626
Unreal.

657
00:39:54,692 --> 00:39:57,262
Hey, you're really something else.

658
00:40:05,203 --> 00:40:08,606
Found it! "How to Grow Cabbages."

659
00:40:08,673 --> 00:40:10,441
It says to plow the field first.

660
00:40:10,508 --> 00:40:12,877
Plow the field? How?

661
00:40:13,578 --> 00:40:16,381
It says we need to make
ridges and furrows.

662
00:40:16,447 --> 00:40:17,682
What's that?

663
00:40:17,749 --> 00:40:19,617
Uh, well, it means…

664
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:22,020
Raised beds and trenches?

665
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:24,055
What's a bed and what's a trench?

666
00:40:24,122 --> 00:40:26,958
Hey, a trench is like this.

667
00:40:27,025 --> 00:40:29,260
It's dug out in a U-shape like this.

668
00:40:29,327 --> 00:40:31,362
T… Trench, that kind of vibe?

669
00:40:32,630 --> 00:40:34,799
Oh! That's right!

670
00:40:34,866 --> 00:40:37,235
It says a trench dips down!
How did you know?

671
00:40:40,171 --> 00:40:41,372
Well…

672
00:40:41,439 --> 00:40:43,541
It just sounds like a trench.

673
00:40:43,608 --> 00:40:45,376
Trench, like a trench.

674
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:47,312
Wow, a total farming prodigy!

675
00:40:47,378 --> 00:40:48,813
Then what's a raised bed?

676
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,081
Forget it, that's enough.

677
00:40:50,148 --> 00:40:51,716
How long will you look it up?

678
00:40:51,783 --> 00:40:53,685
We just plow the field, right?

679
00:40:53,751 --> 00:40:55,253
Let's just dig it all up!

680
00:40:55,320 --> 00:40:56,821
-How?
-Who do you think we are?

681
00:40:56,888 --> 00:40:58,456
We're the gods of shoveling.

682
00:40:58,523 --> 00:41:00,825
We're Republic of Korea
Army reservists!

683
00:41:00,892 --> 00:41:02,994
If the four of us dig away,

684
00:41:03,061 --> 00:41:06,597
half a day will be plenty, right?

685
00:41:06,664 --> 00:41:08,967
Come on, show me what you've got!

686
00:41:23,781 --> 00:41:26,851
At this rate, it'll only take
an hour or two!

687
00:41:27,719 --> 00:41:31,689
Love comes before I even know it

688
00:41:31,756 --> 00:41:35,760
Love comes ever so gently

689
00:41:47,138 --> 00:41:50,441
We shoveled for over three hours,

690
00:41:51,909 --> 00:41:55,113
and we haven't even done a tenth of it.

691
00:41:56,881 --> 00:41:58,082
This won't work.

692
00:41:58,850 --> 00:42:01,519
No way, this is totally impossible.

693
00:42:04,489 --> 00:42:07,158
Um… How did your grandma

694
00:42:07,225 --> 00:42:11,195
ever dig this whole place up
all by herself?

695
00:42:14,966 --> 00:42:17,735
I don't know, I have no idea.

696
00:42:24,642 --> 00:42:25,977
What's that?

697
00:42:26,744 --> 00:42:31,015
With that, we could plow the field
in half a day!

698
00:42:31,082 --> 00:42:35,319
Forget half a day!
We'd be done in an hour!

699
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:37,688
-Should I try borrowing it?
-Sure.

700
00:42:43,661 --> 00:42:46,197
No! Hey, no way, absolutely not!

701
00:42:47,365 --> 00:42:50,201
Hey, how can you give up
without even trying?

702
00:42:50,268 --> 00:42:52,136
I'll go talk to him.

703
00:43:02,780 --> 00:43:03,915
Hello!

704
00:43:03,981 --> 00:43:05,450
We're farming over there.

705
00:43:05,516 --> 00:43:07,018
Please lend us your tractor.

706
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:08,352
-Are you nuts?
-No, sir.

707
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:09,654
-Are you crazy?
-No, sir.

708
00:43:09,720 --> 00:43:12,090
Please lend it to us just once.

709
00:43:12,156 --> 00:43:14,092
He's doing great, nice job.

710
00:43:18,229 --> 00:43:19,430
-Understood.
-Get lost!

711
00:43:19,497 --> 00:43:21,132
Yes, I'm very sorry.

712
00:43:21,199 --> 00:43:23,201
-Get lost, you bastard!
-I'm so sorry.

713
00:43:23,267 --> 00:43:24,735
That little punk.

714
00:43:24,802 --> 00:43:26,737
He's crazy, a total nutjob.

715
00:43:26,804 --> 00:43:28,072
Here he comes!

716
00:43:28,139 --> 00:43:29,907
-Did he get it?
-He's smiling!

717
00:43:29,974 --> 00:43:31,709
-It worked!
-Hey!

718
00:43:31,776 --> 00:43:32,844
Hyeok!

719
00:43:32,910 --> 00:43:34,846
What'd he say? How'd you get it?

720
00:43:34,912 --> 00:43:36,547
-How did you get it?
-Good job.

721
00:43:36,614 --> 00:43:38,049
Be quiet. What'd he say?

722
00:43:38,116 --> 00:43:40,118
Well… He told us to get lost.

723
00:43:42,520 --> 00:43:45,890
What? Then why did you talk
for so long?

724
00:43:45,957 --> 00:43:48,493
He looked ready to hit me,
so I begged for mercy.

725
00:43:48,559 --> 00:43:51,295
Wow, that guy has a fierce temper.

726
00:43:56,267 --> 00:43:58,035
Can we borrow one elsewhere?

727
00:43:58,102 --> 00:44:01,539
Forget it. Everyone in town
has us blacklisted, remember?

728
00:44:01,606 --> 00:44:03,875
Wait! There's your first love!

729
00:44:03,941 --> 00:44:04,876
Yun-hui?

730
00:44:04,942 --> 00:44:06,777
The Village Head must have one.

731
00:44:06,844 --> 00:44:08,713
No, no, no way!

732
00:44:08,779 --> 00:44:11,983
I bragged so loud to her yesterday.
How could I ask?

733
00:44:12,049 --> 00:44:13,718
No way, never!

734
00:44:13,784 --> 00:44:15,753
Does your pride matter right now?

735
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:17,755
Giving up farming and the album?

736
00:44:17,822 --> 00:44:19,624
Well… That's not it, but…

737
00:44:20,158 --> 00:44:24,195
Come on, man, a guy has his pride.

738
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:31,335
Fine, take care then.
I'm going back to Seoul.

739
00:44:31,402 --> 00:44:32,670
-Hey, wait!
-I'm going too.

740
00:44:32,737 --> 00:44:35,139
-Hey!
-Farming was impossible for us.

741
00:44:35,206 --> 00:44:36,274
Bye!

742
00:44:36,340 --> 00:44:38,743
I'm coming too! Shoveling's no fun.

743
00:44:38,809 --> 00:44:40,378
Hey, where are you going?

744
00:44:40,444 --> 00:44:42,346
Hey, where are you going? Hey!

745
00:44:42,413 --> 00:44:45,116
Ma'am, make sure that spot
is spotless, okay?

746
00:44:45,183 --> 00:44:46,918
Got it.

747
00:44:46,984 --> 00:44:49,921
Man-gu, is this really the time
to be drinking that?

748
00:44:49,987 --> 00:44:52,156
It's dusty. Go get water, hurry!

749
00:44:52,223 --> 00:44:54,091
Gosh, hurry up!

750
00:44:55,159 --> 00:44:56,093
Sang-deuk!

751
00:44:56,160 --> 00:44:58,196
Can you give Kkotdori a bath later?

752
00:44:58,262 --> 00:45:00,231
He can't smell when the
County Governor gets here.

753
00:45:00,298 --> 00:45:02,066
Sure, got it.

754
00:45:08,940 --> 00:45:10,608
Yes, hello?

755
00:45:10,675 --> 00:45:12,109
Yes.

756
00:45:12,176 --> 00:45:14,111
Oh, my! Hello, Ms. Secretary!

757
00:45:14,178 --> 00:45:15,513
Yes, Village Head.

758
00:45:15,580 --> 00:45:17,848
The County Governor will leave
in two hours.

759
00:45:17,915 --> 00:45:20,918
Newspaper reporters and local TV
cameras are coming too,

760
00:45:20,985 --> 00:45:22,119
so please be ready.

761
00:45:22,186 --> 00:45:24,055
Oh, please don't worry at all!

762
00:45:24,121 --> 00:45:26,090
We've been cleaning
nonstop since dawn!

763
00:45:26,757 --> 00:45:27,692
Thank you.

764
00:45:27,758 --> 00:45:29,660
I will call you again
when we depart.

765
00:45:29,727 --> 00:45:31,462
Yes, understood. See you soon!

766
00:45:31,529 --> 00:45:32,997
Yes, yes.

767
00:45:36,801 --> 00:45:38,102
WELCOME, COUNTY GOVERNOR

768
00:45:38,169 --> 00:45:41,272
Gosh, why did that fall?
That's such a bad omen.

769
00:45:47,912 --> 00:45:49,814
What brings you here?

770
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:53,451
I was just passing by
and stopped in.

771
00:45:56,120 --> 00:45:58,356
Why is the County Governor
coming here?

772
00:45:58,422 --> 00:46:01,259
Our Kkotdori was chosen as
the Indi County mascot.

773
00:46:02,460 --> 00:46:04,996
-Kkotdori?
-This guy right here.

774
00:46:06,264 --> 00:46:07,331
Oh.

775
00:46:08,666 --> 00:46:10,401
Need a hand with anything else?

776
00:46:10,468 --> 00:46:12,737
Why are you suddenly
acting so fishy?

777
00:46:12,803 --> 00:46:14,405
You want something from me?

778
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:17,608
No, nothing like that.

779
00:46:17,675 --> 00:46:19,644
Really? Never mind, then.

780
00:46:19,710 --> 00:46:22,813
-Lend me your tractor.
-What? My tractor?

781
00:46:22,880 --> 00:46:26,017
-Why?
-I have to plow the field,

782
00:46:26,083 --> 00:46:28,252
and shovels won't cut it at all.

783
00:46:28,319 --> 00:46:31,889
Oh, my! Didn't His Majesty say
he had no need for my help?

784
00:46:31,956 --> 00:46:35,092
Didn't you say you could manage
perfectly well on your own?

785
00:46:35,693 --> 00:46:38,296
Okay, I went a little too far
yesterday, right?

786
00:46:38,362 --> 00:46:41,632
Come on, Yun-hui, please lend me
the tractor, huh? Please?

787
00:46:41,699 --> 00:46:45,236
No, thank you. Do go and manage
perfectly well on your own.

788
00:46:45,303 --> 00:46:46,871
Forget it! Seriously!

789
00:46:46,937 --> 00:46:49,940
I must be a crazy idiot
for asking you for a favor!

790
00:46:50,007 --> 00:46:51,709
Seriously!

791
00:46:54,445 --> 00:46:57,448
-Hey, Lee Min-gi!
-What? What? What?

792
00:46:57,515 --> 00:46:59,016
You're paying for the gas.

793
00:47:01,285 --> 00:47:02,853
So you're lending it to me?

794
00:47:04,088 --> 00:47:06,724
Let me give you a massage right here.

795
00:47:06,791 --> 00:47:09,360
-Ow!
-Your shoulders are so tense.

796
00:47:09,427 --> 00:47:11,228
Ow, get off me, seriously!

797
00:47:15,866 --> 00:47:17,902
You're plowing the field like this?

798
00:47:18,569 --> 00:47:21,138
You have to spread compost first
before plowing the soil!

799
00:47:21,205 --> 00:47:24,041
Compost? What's that?

800
00:47:24,108 --> 00:47:26,110
You're driving me crazy, seriously.

801
00:47:26,977 --> 00:47:30,047
All right, listen up.

802
00:47:30,114 --> 00:47:31,916
Say you're a baby.

803
00:47:31,982 --> 00:47:35,653
To grow up, you need to drink
Mommy's boobie milk full of nutrients.

804
00:47:35,720 --> 00:47:39,357
If Mommy starves and no boobie milk
comes out, what happens?

805
00:47:40,658 --> 00:47:41,859
I'd starve to death.

806
00:47:41,926 --> 00:47:44,428
Right, the soil is the same way.

807
00:47:44,495 --> 00:47:46,997
You have to give the soil
enough nutrients

808
00:47:47,064 --> 00:47:49,834
for radishes and cabbages
to shoot right up, okay?

809
00:47:49,900 --> 00:47:51,669
Oh!

810
00:47:51,736 --> 00:47:54,839
So for cabbages to grow,

811
00:47:54,905 --> 00:47:57,608
this soil is Mommy's boobie,
is that it?

812
00:47:57,675 --> 00:48:00,211
-Right.
-Okay.

813
00:48:01,879 --> 00:48:03,714
Then what's compost?

814
00:48:05,416 --> 00:48:07,451
You're driving me nuts, seriously!

815
00:48:10,221 --> 00:48:12,656
Gosh, this is going to take all night.

816
00:48:12,723 --> 00:48:15,126
Throw it on generously!
Can't you pick up the pace?

817
00:48:20,064 --> 00:48:22,400
-Hey, just dump it out!
-Hey, wait, wait!

818
00:48:22,466 --> 00:48:24,835
We're done. We hauled it all.

819
00:48:26,337 --> 00:48:28,406
We're done, hauled it all.

820
00:48:29,707 --> 00:48:30,975
Is that right?

821
00:48:31,041 --> 00:48:35,079
Then I shall plow the field,
and you shall pick out the stones.

822
00:48:35,146 --> 00:48:36,981
Who is she, Han Seok-bong's mom?

823
00:48:37,047 --> 00:48:39,183
Why pick out stones now?

824
00:48:39,250 --> 00:48:40,451
Excuse me?

825
00:48:40,518 --> 00:48:43,854
If it's full of stones, will the
cabbages grow well or not?

826
00:48:43,921 --> 00:48:45,322
Suit yourselves, then.

827
00:48:45,389 --> 00:48:46,757
Okay, fine.

828
00:48:46,824 --> 00:48:48,592
Fine, we'll clear the rocks, jeez.

829
00:48:56,367 --> 00:48:59,503
Kkotdori, let's take a bath
with your big brother.

830
00:48:59,570 --> 00:49:02,807
I even snuck out my mom's shampoo.

831
00:49:05,910 --> 00:49:06,977
Kkotdori?

832
00:49:09,180 --> 00:49:13,050
Oh no, this little punk
ran away from home again.

833
00:49:13,651 --> 00:49:15,586
I'm losing my mind, seriously.

834
00:49:15,653 --> 00:49:16,921
Kkotdori!

835
00:49:21,025 --> 00:49:21,992
Kkotdori!

836
00:49:28,799 --> 00:49:30,501
This is exhausting, jeez.

837
00:49:33,571 --> 00:49:35,172
This is killing me.

838
00:49:35,940 --> 00:49:39,310
Why is it so much work
just to grow some cabbages?

839
00:49:39,376 --> 00:49:42,246
Isn't the Village Head so cool, though?

840
00:49:42,313 --> 00:49:46,283
She knows farming inside and out,
and she drives a tractor like a pro.

841
00:49:46,350 --> 00:49:47,785
A total femme fatale.

842
00:49:47,852 --> 00:49:50,888
No, wait.
A farm fatale! A farm fatale.

843
00:49:50,955 --> 00:49:53,390
Farm fatale, my foot.
What nonsense.

844
00:49:53,457 --> 00:49:56,827
She's a tomboy and as prickly
as a steel scouring pad.

845
00:49:56,894 --> 00:49:59,163
Why is she taking so long
in the bathroom?

846
00:50:01,365 --> 00:50:02,299
Should I try it?

847
00:50:02,366 --> 00:50:04,001
Hey, don't! Stop, forget it!

848
00:50:04,068 --> 00:50:06,804
Don't cause more trouble.
Just stay still!

849
00:50:06,871 --> 00:50:09,306
-Please.
-It's fine, it's fine.

850
00:50:09,373 --> 00:50:11,809
I have a Class 1 license!
Seven years, zero accidents.

851
00:50:11,876 --> 00:50:13,711
Don't, don't! Seriously, stop!

852
00:50:13,777 --> 00:50:15,613
Give it a shot! Sounds fun.

853
00:50:18,382 --> 00:50:19,850
Why not? It could be fun.

854
00:50:19,917 --> 00:50:23,053
-There he goes again…
-Why are you always so negative?

855
00:50:24,188 --> 00:50:25,823
Is it like a car?

856
00:50:30,294 --> 00:50:32,263
Unbelievable, seriously.

857
00:50:34,265 --> 00:50:36,267
Get down, get down, get down!

858
00:50:36,834 --> 00:50:37,902
All clear!

859
00:50:37,968 --> 00:50:40,271
Hey, hey, stop!

860
00:50:40,337 --> 00:50:41,305
Perfect, nailed it!

861
00:50:41,372 --> 00:50:43,240
Hey!

862
00:50:45,776 --> 00:50:48,012
Stop! Stop! Hey, hey!

863
00:50:48,078 --> 00:50:50,581
What's wrong with this thing?

864
00:50:50,648 --> 00:50:52,149
Stop!

865
00:50:52,216 --> 00:50:54,285
Move! It won't stop!

866
00:50:54,351 --> 00:50:55,619
It won't stop!

867
00:50:55,686 --> 00:50:56,787
Hey, hey, hey!

868
00:50:57,955 --> 00:50:59,490
Out of the way!

869
00:51:22,379 --> 00:51:24,782
-What the heck!
-Seriously, that guy.

870
00:51:24,848 --> 00:51:27,351
What are you doing, man?
We almost died!

871
00:51:27,418 --> 00:51:29,787
-Seriously!
-Jeez, man.

872
00:51:30,688 --> 00:51:32,189
What was that?

873
00:51:32,256 --> 00:51:36,293
I just got a really bad feeling
about that.

874
00:51:39,697 --> 00:51:42,333
It felt like I hit something.

875
00:51:47,004 --> 00:51:49,773
Min-gi, you okay? Why are you…

876
00:51:50,908 --> 00:51:52,409
Hey, what's wrong?

877
00:51:56,714 --> 00:51:58,782
Hey, this… Did you do this?

878
00:51:58,849 --> 00:52:00,150
I think he did.

879
00:52:00,217 --> 00:52:01,285
Is it dead?

880
00:52:01,352 --> 00:52:04,355
Wait, why is a deer
wearing a necklace…

881
00:52:05,122 --> 00:52:07,157
Wait, wait, hold on.

882
00:52:07,224 --> 00:52:09,727
Isn't that a phoenix emblem?

883
00:52:10,361 --> 00:52:12,630
Huh? It really is a phoenix.

884
00:52:12,696 --> 00:52:16,433
A phoenix means the Blue House…

885
00:52:18,469 --> 00:52:21,505
What? The Blue House?

886
00:52:23,674 --> 00:52:24,808
That necklace… Right.

887
00:52:24,875 --> 00:52:27,144
Right, President Roh Moo-hyun

888
00:52:27,211 --> 00:52:30,481
came here in person
and put that on it.

889
00:52:36,420 --> 00:52:39,857
I think this is that descendant
of the Jeong-ipum-rok

890
00:52:39,923 --> 00:52:41,525
by the village entrance.

891
00:52:41,592 --> 00:52:45,629
They said it was just chosen
as the Indi County mascot.

892
00:52:45,696 --> 00:52:48,198
The County Governor is coming today
for the ceremony.

893
00:52:48,265 --> 00:52:50,668
-We're screwed.
-I told you not to do it!

894
00:52:50,734 --> 00:52:51,935
Why does everything go wrong?

895
00:52:52,703 --> 00:52:53,704
We're done for.

896
00:52:53,771 --> 00:52:57,207
If we get caught, we'll get
kicked out for sure.

897
00:52:57,274 --> 00:52:58,676
No way.

898
00:52:58,742 --> 00:53:02,012
We can never get kicked out.

899
00:53:04,515 --> 00:53:06,050
This thing…

900
00:53:06,850 --> 00:53:08,385
Let's hide it.

901
00:53:08,952 --> 00:53:09,820
What?

902
00:53:09,887 --> 00:53:11,855
Yes, yes, of course. I understand.

903
00:53:11,922 --> 00:53:14,458
Yes, I will see you shortly. Goodbye.

904
00:53:15,059 --> 00:53:17,494
Oh, my gosh. It's already this late.

905
00:53:18,162 --> 00:53:21,432
Wait, now what? Hey, what's up?

906
00:53:22,566 --> 00:53:24,668
What? Kkotdori escaped again?

907
00:53:24,735 --> 00:53:27,371
Gosh, I told you to fix
that darn pen, seriously!

908
00:53:27,438 --> 00:53:31,675
Gosh, the County Governor already left.
We're in big trouble now.

909
00:53:31,742 --> 00:53:33,210
I'll be right there,

910
00:53:33,277 --> 00:53:35,312
so get the villagers
and look for Kkotdori!

911
00:53:35,379 --> 00:53:37,147
Okay, got it.

912
00:53:39,616 --> 00:53:43,487
Where did those punks run off to
in the middle of work, seriously?

913
00:53:44,855 --> 00:53:47,224
No, wait. I don't have time for this.

914
00:53:47,291 --> 00:53:49,993
Kkotdori! Kkotdori!

915
00:53:50,060 --> 00:53:51,995
It's downhill! Slow down!

916
00:53:52,062 --> 00:53:53,664
Slow down! Look out!

917
00:53:59,737 --> 00:54:01,105
Ow, my balls!

918
00:54:05,342 --> 00:54:07,244
Guys! Hurry, get over here!

919
00:54:08,445 --> 00:54:10,380
-Hey!
-A deer!

920
00:54:13,350 --> 00:54:14,752
I told you to slow down!

921
00:54:14,818 --> 00:54:16,787
Darn it, load the deer up, hurry!

922
00:54:16,854 --> 00:54:18,789
Come on, hurry and load it up!

923
00:54:19,690 --> 00:54:21,058
What? What?

924
00:54:21,125 --> 00:54:22,726
-What is it?
-The deer and I made eye contact!

925
00:54:22,793 --> 00:54:25,028
So what if you made eye contact? Hurry!

926
00:54:25,095 --> 00:54:27,030
-Hurry, lift it!
-Cover its eyes, quick!

927
00:54:27,097 --> 00:54:28,932
I said cover its eyes, hurry!

928
00:54:28,999 --> 00:54:30,434
Cover its eyes first, darn it!

929
00:54:30,501 --> 00:54:32,369
Hurry, come on! Move!

930
00:54:32,436 --> 00:54:34,805
Kkotdori! Kkotdori!

931
00:54:41,478 --> 00:54:45,182
All right, next up,
sharp turn Course B past the old man.

932
00:54:45,249 --> 00:54:46,183
-Let's go!
-Sharp turn!

933
00:54:46,250 --> 00:54:47,684
Keep up the good work, sir!

934
00:54:47,751 --> 00:54:50,287
Nice! All right, next, full speed ahead!

935
00:54:50,354 --> 00:54:52,589
All right, full speed again!

936
00:54:52,656 --> 00:54:54,191
-Nice job!
-Kkotdori!

937
00:54:55,459 --> 00:54:57,795
-Kkotdori!

938
00:54:59,663 --> 00:55:01,965
-Kkotdori!

939
00:55:02,032 --> 00:55:05,302
Where on earth did this thing go? Gosh.

940
00:55:10,340 --> 00:55:12,075
Hold still, you little punk.

941
00:55:20,951 --> 00:55:23,086
Villagers are swarming everywhere!

942
00:55:23,153 --> 00:55:24,955
We'll get caught any minute, man.

943
00:55:25,022 --> 00:55:27,191
Look, now that it's come to this,

944
00:55:27,858 --> 00:55:29,293
let's get out of the village.

945
00:55:29,359 --> 00:55:30,527
Hurry up and push!

946
00:55:30,594 --> 00:55:32,095
-Let's go!
-Where? Where to?

947
00:55:32,162 --> 00:55:33,764
Kkotdori!

948
00:55:33,831 --> 00:55:35,399
Oh, Kkotdori!

949
00:55:36,867 --> 00:55:39,069
Ow! Oh, my butt!

950
00:55:39,136 --> 00:55:40,671
Ugh, my butt…

951
00:55:40,737 --> 00:55:43,073
-Yoon-hee!
-Darn it, you guys, seriously!

952
00:55:47,077 --> 00:55:50,013
-I'm sorry.
-Watch where you're going, seriously!

953
00:55:50,647 --> 00:55:52,082
I wondered where you went,

954
00:55:52,149 --> 00:55:53,917
and what are you doing here?

955
00:55:55,219 --> 00:55:56,687
Wait, hold on, that's right.

956
00:55:56,753 --> 00:55:58,689
Have you guys seen Kkotdori?

957
00:55:59,923 --> 00:56:02,492
Huh? Uh, no, I haven't.

958
00:56:02,559 --> 00:56:03,994
Uh, why?

959
00:56:04,061 --> 00:56:07,164
We're in real trouble.
Our Kkotdori is missing!

960
00:56:07,231 --> 00:56:08,699
The County Governor is due soon.

961
00:56:08,765 --> 00:56:11,301
This is a real disaster, seriously.

962
00:56:12,769 --> 00:56:14,972
Wait, what's that?

963
00:56:16,240 --> 00:56:19,610
-Uh, um… Laundry.
-Laundry?

964
00:56:19,676 --> 00:56:21,778
Why are you hauling laundry in a cart?

965
00:56:22,546 --> 00:56:24,248
Whoa, hold on, hold on.

966
00:56:24,314 --> 00:56:26,717
We have so much,
we're taking it to the cleaner's in town.

967
00:56:26,783 --> 00:56:27,918
In town?

968
00:56:27,985 --> 00:56:30,520
That's over 40 minutes away by bus,

969
00:56:30,587 --> 00:56:32,689
and you're hauling a cart all the way?

970
00:56:32,756 --> 00:56:33,891
Yes!

971
00:56:35,325 --> 00:56:36,860
It's great exercise, too!

972
00:56:37,527 --> 00:56:38,795
Oh, I love it!

973
00:56:39,463 --> 00:56:41,398
Gosh, forget it, stop.

974
00:56:41,465 --> 00:56:43,166
I'll just run it in my washer.

975
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:45,302
-No, don't!
-Gosh, you scared me!

976
00:56:45,369 --> 00:56:47,771
Why are you yelling like a maniac?
Are you crazy?

977
00:56:50,574 --> 00:56:53,343
No, uh, that's not it.

978
00:56:53,410 --> 00:56:55,212
It's our underwear, you see.

979
00:56:56,546 --> 00:56:58,448
Every single bit of this?

980
00:56:58,515 --> 00:56:59,983
Yes.

981
00:57:00,050 --> 00:57:02,119
-How embarrassing.
-Tell me about it.

982
00:57:02,853 --> 00:57:05,889
Right. Several times a day,

983
00:57:05,956 --> 00:57:07,791
we make sure to change our briefs.

984
00:57:07,858 --> 00:57:09,326
So embarrassing.

985
00:57:09,393 --> 00:57:11,695
-So embarrassing.
-It's fine.

986
00:57:11,762 --> 00:57:15,933
I can't tell if you guys
are neat freaks or just weird.

987
00:57:16,667 --> 00:57:18,568
You handle that yourselves.

988
00:57:18,635 --> 00:57:21,371
Anyway, if you see Kkotdori,
be sure to call me.

989
00:57:21,438 --> 00:57:23,373
-Got it?
-Right, sure.

990
00:57:23,440 --> 00:57:25,275
-Of course.
-I'm off, then.

991
00:57:25,342 --> 00:57:26,209
Take care.

992
00:57:26,276 --> 00:57:28,011
Goodbye.

993
00:58:04,014 --> 00:58:04,881
We're doomed.

994
00:58:09,052 --> 00:58:12,222
Kkotdori… Kkot…

995
00:58:12,289 --> 00:58:15,258
You punk, what did you just
do to Kkotdori?

996
00:58:16,026 --> 00:58:17,828
Calm down and hear me out.

997
00:58:17,894 --> 00:58:19,463
It was an accident!

998
00:58:19,529 --> 00:58:22,432
He jumped right in front
of the tractor, I swear!

999
00:58:22,499 --> 00:58:23,934
Please believe me!

1000
00:58:24,001 --> 00:58:26,370
I'm really sorry!
I'm so sorry!

1001
00:58:26,436 --> 00:58:29,306
Will an apology fix a disaster
like this?

1002
00:58:29,373 --> 00:58:32,175
Oh, no! I don't want to know!

1003
00:58:32,242 --> 00:58:33,643
This is all on you!

1004
00:58:33,710 --> 00:58:36,313
This is on you, you punk!
If you don't fix this,

1005
00:58:36,380 --> 00:58:40,083
forget getting kicked out of town,
the villagers will beat you to death!

1006
00:58:40,984 --> 00:58:43,320
Please save my life just this once!

1007
00:58:44,287 --> 00:58:46,223
I'm begging you on my knees!

1008
00:58:46,957 --> 00:58:48,492
Good grief.

1009
00:58:48,558 --> 00:58:51,995
The truth is…

1010
00:58:52,062 --> 00:58:55,165
I'm neither a singer nor famous.

1011
00:58:56,600 --> 00:58:57,768
I hit rock bottom in Seoul,

1012
00:58:57,834 --> 00:59:00,003
and came down here
to farm cabbages.

1013
00:59:00,070 --> 00:59:01,705
What?

1014
00:59:02,472 --> 00:59:06,676
I really need to farm cabbages
and make money.

1015
00:59:06,743 --> 00:59:09,346
So I can put out an album
and my debt…

1016
00:59:11,915 --> 00:59:13,383
Wait, what?

1017
00:59:14,885 --> 00:59:19,823
Anyway, I really have to
farm cabbages!

1018
00:59:19,890 --> 00:59:20,757
Please?

1019
00:59:20,824 --> 00:59:24,795
Oh, no, leave me out of it!
You deal with it yourself!

1020
00:59:27,130 --> 00:59:28,999
Are you really going
to be this petty?

1021
00:59:29,066 --> 00:59:31,068
You can't treat the man
who saved your life like this!

1022
00:59:31,134 --> 00:59:33,336
Saved my life?
What are you talking about?

1023
00:59:33,403 --> 00:59:35,739
I saved you when you fell
into the stream!

1024
00:59:35,806 --> 00:59:36,873
Don't you remember?

1025
00:59:36,940 --> 00:59:41,144
Are you seriously blackmailing me
with that right now? How pathetic!

1026
00:59:41,211 --> 00:59:44,181
Then don't make me act pathetic
and just help me out!

1027
00:59:44,247 --> 00:59:46,283
What do you expect me to do
when it's already dead?

1028
00:59:46,349 --> 00:59:47,851
Can I raise the dead?

1029
00:59:47,918 --> 00:59:50,087
This is driving me crazy!

1030
00:59:50,153 --> 00:59:51,188
Is there no way?

1031
00:59:51,254 --> 00:59:52,656
I'm losing my mind.

1032
00:59:53,290 --> 00:59:57,394
Um, aren't we the only ones
who know he's dead?

1033
00:59:57,461 --> 01:00:00,630
All deer look pretty much alike,
so no one will tell the difference.

1034
01:00:00,697 --> 01:00:02,632
What are you getting at?

1035
01:00:03,967 --> 01:00:08,138
Are you saying we should swap him
with another deer?

1036
01:00:08,205 --> 01:00:09,539
Where would we get a deer?

1037
01:00:09,606 --> 01:00:11,007
We have one.

1038
01:00:11,875 --> 01:00:13,410
We have one at home!

1039
01:00:21,251 --> 01:00:24,054
Why on earth is there a deer
in your room?

1040
01:00:24,121 --> 01:00:26,356
Beats me, he was here from the start.

1041
01:00:27,257 --> 01:00:29,593
Still, he and that Kkotdori…

1042
01:00:29,659 --> 01:00:31,361
They look this much alike,

1043
01:00:31,428 --> 01:00:33,296
so no one will know if we swap…

1044
01:00:33,363 --> 01:00:34,764
That makes no sense!

1045
01:00:35,432 --> 01:00:38,268
Fine, even if I give in
and say we swap them,

1046
01:00:38,335 --> 01:00:40,103
how are you going to move him?

1047
01:00:40,170 --> 01:00:43,807
A wild deer is completely
impossible to control.

1048
01:00:43,874 --> 01:00:46,209
Like a runaway train
with broken brakes,

1049
01:00:46,276 --> 01:00:48,011
he's a terrifying beast.

1050
01:00:49,546 --> 01:00:50,714
Don't worry about that.

1051
01:00:50,780 --> 01:00:52,916
We'll take care of it.

1052
01:00:52,983 --> 01:00:54,618
Let's go!

1053
01:00:58,488 --> 01:01:00,924
Come on, you cowards!
Hurry up! Get over here!

1054
01:01:06,396 --> 01:01:08,498
Get over here, hurry up!

1055
01:01:08,565 --> 01:01:10,534
Hurry, hurry!

1056
01:01:10,600 --> 01:01:13,236
Han-cheol, you grab the antlers!
Grab them, quick!

1057
01:01:13,303 --> 01:01:15,539
Get ready! On the count of three!
One, two, three!

1058
01:01:15,605 --> 01:01:17,073
One, two, three!

1059
01:01:26,816 --> 01:01:28,985
Oh, no. The County Governor
will be here any minute.

1060
01:01:29,052 --> 01:01:32,122
What do we do if we can't find
our Kkotdori?

1061
01:01:32,189 --> 01:01:33,924
So much for the paved road.

1062
01:01:33,990 --> 01:01:35,125
WELCOME, COUNTY GOVERNOR

1063
01:01:35,192 --> 01:01:37,227
Wait, where on earth
did Yun-hui run off to?

1064
01:01:37,294 --> 01:01:39,663
The County Governor
should be here by now.

1065
01:01:39,729 --> 01:01:42,098
Looking for Kkotdori, probably.

1066
01:01:42,165 --> 01:01:44,100
Seriously, they're so slow.

1067
01:01:44,167 --> 01:01:46,770
That guy is always
so negative about everything.

1068
01:01:46,836 --> 01:01:48,338
Oh, my! He's here!

1069
01:01:48,405 --> 01:01:50,273
-We're in trouble now!
-Oh, no!

1070
01:02:07,224 --> 01:02:09,960
My apologies.
I am a little late.

1071
01:02:10,026 --> 01:02:11,194
That is quite all right.

1072
01:02:11,261 --> 01:02:14,231
You are busy with public affairs,
so I understand.

1073
01:02:14,297 --> 01:02:15,699
Thank you for understanding.

1074
01:02:15,765 --> 01:02:18,034
Then shall we take a look
at our mascot first?

1075
01:02:18,101 --> 01:02:20,904
Well, you see, Kkotdori is…

1076
01:02:20,971 --> 01:02:22,606
Wait a second!

1077
01:02:25,442 --> 01:02:27,777
I am so sorry we are late.

1078
01:02:33,083 --> 01:02:34,384
Why bring these punks?

1079
01:02:34,451 --> 01:02:37,387
Come on, they're part of
our village family now.

1080
01:02:37,454 --> 01:02:39,022
We have to include them.

1081
01:02:40,523 --> 01:02:42,092
Right?

1082
01:02:47,297 --> 01:02:49,566
Dear residents of Hadurok-ri,

1083
01:02:49,633 --> 01:02:52,902
to be here today to appoint
the bright future of Indi County,

1084
01:02:52,969 --> 01:02:54,004
our proud mascot,

1085
01:02:54,070 --> 01:02:56,506
the Jeong-ipum-rok deer, Kkotdori,

1086
01:02:56,573 --> 01:02:59,276
as the official mascot
of Indi County,

1087
01:02:59,342 --> 01:03:02,412
is truly a great honor for me.

1088
01:03:02,479 --> 01:03:03,913
Now, as for Kkotdori,

1089
01:03:03,980 --> 01:03:05,782
-he is of noble bloodline,
-Hey!

1090
01:03:05,849 --> 01:03:07,284
a sika deer whose ancestor

1091
01:03:07,350 --> 01:03:08,385
in the Joseon Dynasty,

1092
01:03:08,451 --> 01:03:10,387
-fought off barbarians
-Stay still!

1093
01:03:10,453 --> 01:03:13,189
to protect the king,
the most loyal of subjects,

1094
01:03:13,256 --> 01:03:15,258
-a Jeong-ipum-rok deer.
-Hold still!

1095
01:03:15,325 --> 01:03:16,860
Having inherited that courage

1096
01:03:16,926 --> 01:03:18,595
and wisdom, Kkotdori will be

1097
01:03:18,662 --> 01:03:20,530
our Indi County's…

1098
01:03:26,336 --> 01:03:29,372
I walk down

1099
01:03:29,439 --> 01:03:32,842
An endless road

1100
01:03:32,909 --> 01:03:37,881
When my heart longs for you

1101
01:03:39,816 --> 01:03:43,153
The dazzling sunlight

1102
01:03:43,219 --> 01:03:45,989
Brings you back to me

1103
01:03:46,990 --> 01:03:51,394
I get lost in memories

1104
01:03:52,929 --> 01:03:56,533
Where are you now?

1105
01:03:56,599 --> 01:04:00,403
Where are you, my love?

1106
01:04:00,470 --> 01:04:04,174
Are you crying

1107
01:04:04,240 --> 01:04:07,210
Just like me?

1108
01:04:07,277 --> 01:04:10,580
Like the stars and the moon

1109
01:04:10,647 --> 01:04:13,483
Always in the same place…
